WEBVTT

00:09.980 --> 00:11.780
Sunday afternoon.

00:11.780 --> 00:14.980
Bathing while the sun is still high.

00:14.980 --> 00:17.340
What a luxurious thing to do.

00:19.350 --> 00:21.000
Beethoven-senpai...

00:21.750 --> 00:25.670
He hasn't been in the best of moods, ever
since we came back from Bach's place.

00:26.250 --> 00:29.680
Is there anything I can do to help
him take his mind off of things?

00:30.340 --> 00:32.040
But that aside...

00:33.360 --> 00:36.910
I enjoy seeing Mozart in a bad mood.

00:36.910 --> 00:40.100
Such superficial men deserve to be

00:40.100 --> 00:41.430
taken down a notch.

00:41.880 --> 00:43.390
Good job, Bach.

00:55.740 --> 00:58.630
Let's spin super fast!

01:05.830 --> 01:08.040
I was wondering if you'd like to go to
the amusement park with me someday.

01:10.460 --> 01:12.460
Schu-san's in a good mood.

01:12.460 --> 01:15.130
Franz Schubert's "Die Forelle."

01:15.610 --> 01:19.270
One of the most beloved of
lieds, Schubert himself would

01:19.270 --> 01:22.770
eventually go on to arrange
it for piano quintet as well.

01:35.390 --> 01:36.710
Wait, what?

01:37.240 --> 01:38.030
What the?

01:38.390 --> 01:39.720
What just happened?

01:40.380 --> 01:41.480
Where am I?

01:41.480 --> 01:42.870
In the bath?

01:43.290 --> 01:44.810
Did I sink?

01:45.250 --> 01:46.280
Not good.

01:46.280 --> 01:48.280
I don't want to drown.

01:48.580 --> 01:50.180
I have to stand up.

01:50.520 --> 01:51.260
Yes.

01:51.260 --> 01:52.760
Stand up.

01:53.100 --> 01:54.100
It's easy.

01:54.100 --> 01:57.200
I just put my hand on the side
of the bathtub, and up we go.

01:58.580 --> 02:00.410
Put my hand on the bathtub...

02:00.850 --> 02:02.680
My hand... Huh?

02:03.160 --> 02:05.060
My hand. Where's my hand?

02:05.380 --> 02:06.990
Wait a second, stay calm.

02:06.990 --> 02:08.510
I just need to stand up.

02:08.510 --> 02:11.390
Extend my legs, and up we go.

02:11.690 --> 02:12.530
Legs...

02:13.610 --> 02:15.240
Hands... Legs...

03:54.880 --> 03:59.170
13: "Die Forelle"

03:54.950 --> 03:57.030
What the... What's going on?

03:58.110 --> 04:00.030
What's become of me?

04:00.420 --> 04:02.010
I can't see myself.

04:06.970 --> 04:08.190
I-I saw!

04:08.190 --> 04:09.810
I didn't want to see that.

04:10.340 --> 04:13.200
A fish. I've become a fish.

04:13.870 --> 04:16.620
No wonder I'm not struggling
to breathe underwater.

04:16.920 --> 04:18.160
But why?

04:18.630 --> 04:19.530
No...

04:21.210 --> 04:22.530
That's it!

04:22.530 --> 04:24.640
I swung a baton and activated my Musik.

04:25.160 --> 04:27.130
What an amazing ability.

04:28.040 --> 04:29.620
But what use could it be?

04:29.960 --> 04:33.120
No, first of all, what am I supposed to do?

04:33.500 --> 04:34.540
Maybe with the baton...

04:34.540 --> 04:38.440
Maybe if I activate my Musik
again, I can go back.

04:38.980 --> 04:40.960
Where is my baton?

04:41.920 --> 04:43.460
I can't find it anywhere.

04:43.460 --> 04:46.300
This is bad. This is really bad.

04:46.300 --> 04:47.290
I know.

04:47.290 --> 04:50.260
I should get someone to use their
Musik to change me back to normal.

04:50.260 --> 04:52.680
Somebody! Beethoven-senpai!

04:52.680 --> 04:54.280
Help me!

04:54.280 --> 04:56.350
Liszt! Chopin! Hey!

04:56.350 --> 04:58.020
Spin boost!

04:58.230 --> 04:59.570
Gah!

05:01.470 --> 05:03.240
I messed up again.

05:03.490 --> 05:05.100
Ow...

05:09.350 --> 05:11.040
<i>Him</i>...

05:11.040 --> 05:14.370
I'd rather not be in a position to owe
him anything, but I have no other options.

05:14.630 --> 05:18.260
Mozart, I'll bow down to you just this once.

05:18.560 --> 05:21.690
Bring me back to normal with your Musik.

05:22.500 --> 05:24.340
You look tasty.

05:26.280 --> 05:28.990
Dammit, you fish, you!

05:34.820 --> 05:36.410
It's so fast.

05:36.410 --> 05:37.730
Oh, I know.

05:37.730 --> 05:39.050
I know what to use.

05:39.520 --> 05:42.010
Does he think he's going to eat me?

05:42.010 --> 05:43.950
That barbarian!

05:43.950 --> 05:46.530
Does he not wonder why there's
a fish in the bathtub?

05:47.410 --> 05:49.970
I need to get out, or he'll eat me.

05:49.970 --> 05:51.140
I must escape.

05:51.140 --> 05:52.250
But where?

05:52.250 --> 05:53.540
How?

05:55.760 --> 05:57.130
I can't breathe!

05:57.130 --> 05:58.980
Air! Water!

05:58.980 --> 06:00.920
Take me into water!

06:00.920 --> 06:02.340
Hurry!

06:02.340 --> 06:03.300
A net?

06:03.300 --> 06:05.570
Yeah, for catching fish and stuff.

06:05.570 --> 06:09.200
There used to be one in the closet,
but I don't think it's in there anymore.

06:09.200 --> 06:12.470
Beethes took it to go fishing earlier.

06:14.020 --> 06:15.760
And what are you going to use it for?

06:15.760 --> 06:17.660
There was a fish in the bathtub.

06:17.660 --> 06:18.900
A tasty-looking one.

06:18.900 --> 06:21.580
Why would there be a fish in the bathtub?

06:21.580 --> 06:22.900
There was!

06:23.140 --> 06:25.610
I'm busy right now. Get out of my way.

06:25.610 --> 06:28.760
It stopped raining, so I can finally
hang some laundry outside.

06:28.760 --> 06:31.580
I swear! There really was a fish!

06:31.580 --> 06:33.910
Okay, okay. Good for you.

06:33.910 --> 06:36.210
I'm getting dizzy!

06:36.210 --> 06:37.940
Let go!

06:37.940 --> 06:40.580
You're all mine now.

06:41.460 --> 06:44.170
Why did a fish come out
of the washing machine?

06:44.480 --> 06:46.800
Who cares why?

06:46.800 --> 06:48.380
Hey, how should we eat it?

06:48.670 --> 06:50.390
Is it even edible?

06:50.390 --> 06:52.040
It better not be poisonous.

06:52.040 --> 06:54.450
Dunno. Why don't we try
feeding it to someone?

06:54.450 --> 06:56.230
That's not a good idea.

06:56.230 --> 07:00.520
Oh, Chopin-san might know
about stuff like this, though.

07:01.080 --> 07:02.900
This is very bad.

07:02.900 --> 07:06.340
I'm going to end up their dinner or lunch.

07:06.340 --> 07:07.650
Think.

07:07.650 --> 07:09.800
How do I get out of this predicament?

07:10.240 --> 07:11.530
Think, Franz.

07:11.530 --> 07:12.420
Franz.

07:12.420 --> 07:14.290
I am Franz Schubert.

07:14.710 --> 07:15.830
Hello.

07:15.830 --> 07:16.950
Nice to meet you.

07:16.950 --> 07:18.150
No, what am I talking about?

07:18.450 --> 07:20.640
I need to think about how
to get out of this pinch.

07:20.940 --> 07:22.270
From this pinch.

07:22.270 --> 07:23.260
Pinch...

07:23.260 --> 07:24.070
Pinch...

07:24.070 --> 07:26.960
Panch... Ponch... Fruit punch...

07:27.210 --> 07:28.590
This is an apple.

07:28.590 --> 07:30.110
Is that an apple?

07:30.460 --> 07:33.020
Yes, that is a delicious apple.

07:33.020 --> 07:34.510
Would you like some?

07:34.790 --> 07:35.850
No!

07:35.850 --> 07:38.190
I can't think about anything complex!

07:38.190 --> 07:41.340
I want to, but I just don't
have the brains for it!

07:42.050 --> 07:43.910
How did this happen?

07:45.010 --> 07:46.960
What is going to become of me now?

07:50.400 --> 07:52.400
Stare...

07:53.180 --> 07:56.720
I believe that their Musik is still unstable.

07:57.020 --> 08:00.250
They have power, but they
don't have control over it.

08:00.820 --> 08:04.500
Their Musik doesn't have anywhere
near the polish that yours does.

08:04.860 --> 08:08.550
It wouldn't surprise me if their Musik
ended up being activated by itself,

08:08.550 --> 08:10.920
causing serious trouble.

08:12.150 --> 08:13.320
Um...

08:13.320 --> 08:16.990
Bach-sama, which do you like, fish or meat?

08:17.540 --> 08:18.670
Forte.

08:19.420 --> 08:22.250
Are you pro-mayo-on-takoyaki,

08:22.250 --> 08:23.770
or anti-mayo-on-takoyaki?

08:23.770 --> 08:25.060
Mezzo piano.

08:25.060 --> 08:28.200
Crispy or chewy pizza? Which do you like?

08:28.200 --> 08:29.530
Crescendo.

08:31.360 --> 08:32.350
Why?

08:32.350 --> 08:35.160
Why won't you speak normally
to us, Bach-sama?

08:35.640 --> 08:36.530
Okay...

08:36.530 --> 08:38.320
When you lean your seat
back on the bullet train,

08:38.320 --> 08:40.660
do you say something to the person
behind you, or do you just do it?

08:40.660 --> 08:42.400
Come on, Tchaiko-chan.

08:42.400 --> 08:43.970
You have to stop asking
Bach-sama so many questions.

08:43.970 --> 08:45.790
He wants to finish his meal.

08:46.050 --> 08:47.070
Leave me alone!

08:47.070 --> 08:47.780
But...

08:47.780 --> 08:50.290
I told you to leave me
alone, you one-hit wonder!

08:50.290 --> 08:52.120
Don't call me a one-hit wonder!

08:52.120 --> 08:52.840
Take it back!

08:52.840 --> 08:55.280
I'm not taking it back. One-hit wonder!

08:54.740 --> 08:57.760
I dare you to say that again, beardo!

08:57.200 --> 08:59.150
Oh, more water, sir.

08:57.760 --> 08:59.720
Shut up, blunt bangs!

08:59.720 --> 09:03.140
I was wondering if you'd like to go to
the amusement park with me someday.

09:02.270 --> 09:04.640
I hope Bąda-chan gets back to me soon.

09:05.480 --> 09:08.650
M-Maybe she's busy.

09:09.560 --> 09:11.050
This is the fish.

09:11.050 --> 09:12.780
Brown trout?

09:13.050 --> 09:15.690
Wow, so that's what it's called.

09:15.690 --> 09:18.280
I've never heard of it.
What's it called in Japanese?

09:18.730 --> 09:19.620
Masu.

09:19.620 --> 09:21.100
So it's a masu.

09:21.100 --> 09:23.120
Do you know how to cook it?

09:24.370 --> 09:25.120
How to Cook Trout

09:25.120 --> 09:28.380
How to Cook Trout

09:26.620 --> 09:28.380
They all look so good.

09:29.490 --> 09:31.300
Unless I can go back to being human,

09:31.540 --> 09:34.010
they'll eventually eat me.

09:34.010 --> 09:35.600
I must make a decision.

09:36.200 --> 09:38.900
Yes! I must leave this mansion.

09:39.250 --> 09:41.820
I don't want to part with Beethoven-senpai,

09:41.820 --> 09:45.030
now that I've finally met him,
but I'll adore him from afar.

09:45.600 --> 09:47.820
Goodbye, Beethoven-senpai.

09:47.820 --> 09:51.400
Goodbye, those of you with
whom I lived briefly.

09:51.400 --> 09:54.340
And go to Hell, Mozart!

09:54.340 --> 09:58.240
The moment I jump out of that window
may be the moment that I perish.

09:58.600 --> 10:01.920
But if I must fall, I will
fall in pursuit of a future!

10:06.580 --> 10:07.160
Uh...

10:09.120 --> 10:10.380
A puddle!

10:10.770 --> 10:12.000
I'm saved!

10:12.000 --> 10:13.930
It's because of that rain yesterday.

10:14.960 --> 10:15.880
Great!

10:15.880 --> 10:18.220
I think I can make it to the
entrance of the mansion.

10:27.730 --> 10:28.560
Good.

10:28.560 --> 10:31.260
I've finally made it to
the pond by the gate.

10:31.560 --> 10:32.570
Now...

10:32.570 --> 10:35.390
How do I get out of the gate?

10:40.510 --> 10:42.220
No. Don't do it.

10:42.220 --> 10:43.670
Stay calm, you.

10:43.670 --> 10:45.580
You shouldn't. You'll regret it.

10:45.580 --> 10:46.710
Raw fish are bad, m'kay?

10:46.710 --> 10:49.000
I have parasites. Parasites! No, really!

10:58.140 --> 11:00.100
What's all the racket, Hasshie?

11:01.730 --> 11:03.420
Hey, a fish.

11:03.930 --> 11:05.560
Was there ever a fish here?

11:07.010 --> 11:08.130
Kagura-kun!

11:08.130 --> 11:09.270
You're a savior!

11:09.550 --> 11:11.940
I need him to save me.

11:12.400 --> 11:13.230
All right.

11:19.610 --> 11:20.530
Let's see...

11:24.250 --> 11:27.240
"I want freedom!"

11:32.700 --> 11:34.100
Freedom...

11:34.400 --> 11:37.610
I see. You want freedom!

11:37.610 --> 11:40.010
I get it, you want to get out of this pond

11:40.010 --> 11:42.090
and go swimming somewhere bigger.

11:42.960 --> 11:45.100
Don't worry, fishie.

11:45.810 --> 11:49.190
I'll take you to the bigger world.

11:51.190 --> 11:53.670
Hey, it's gone.

12:06.500 --> 12:08.430
All right, swim along.

12:08.430 --> 12:11.170
It's nothing like the small
world you were in before here.

12:15.460 --> 12:17.100
It looks so happy.

12:17.100 --> 12:17.840
Later.

12:18.650 --> 12:20.350
Be well, man.

12:22.310 --> 12:23.520
I did good.

12:23.520 --> 12:25.320
You're so pure, Sousuke.

12:25.320 --> 12:26.810
You can't make yourself
useful to other people,

12:25.970 --> 12:30.640
*Don't Release Fish Without Permission.

12:26.810 --> 12:28.860
so you try to at least make yourself
useful to other creatures.

12:28.860 --> 12:31.060
That wasn't the idea!

12:33.460 --> 12:36.310
Twinkle, twinkle, little sun...

12:36.310 --> 12:37.400
Wait, no.

12:37.400 --> 12:39.610
What a beautiful sight.

12:40.000 --> 12:41.960
It's as if light and shadow are

12:41.960 --> 12:44.110
competing to show off their magic.

12:44.110 --> 12:47.270
It's so big and great!

12:47.270 --> 12:48.210
Wait, no.

12:48.210 --> 12:50.040
This is my new home.

12:50.500 --> 12:53.190
My second life begins in this

12:53.190 --> 12:55.410
beautiful world of water.

12:55.770 --> 12:57.790
What joy.

12:58.200 --> 13:00.060
I'm hungry.

13:00.060 --> 13:01.530
I'm so hungry.

13:01.530 --> 13:02.660
Wait, no.

13:02.660 --> 13:03.770
Damn it, this is bad.

13:03.770 --> 13:05.980
I'm turning into a fish.

13:05.980 --> 13:08.390
I need to make a life in this world.

13:08.690 --> 13:10.690
First, I need to find some food.

13:27.500 --> 13:28.530
That took no time.

13:30.640 --> 13:31.490
Why?!

13:31.490 --> 13:33.370
Why can't I catch any?

13:34.480 --> 13:37.690
The people around me are
catching them left and right.

13:37.690 --> 13:40.880
Do you not have any intention of taking
my bait, you aquatic bastards?

13:40.880 --> 13:42.010
Very well.

13:42.310 --> 13:43.630
It's a test of will.

13:43.990 --> 13:47.510
I'll surely capture you
with my homemade bait.

13:59.710 --> 14:00.440
Here we go.

14:03.070 --> 14:04.900
Ow, ow, ow...

14:05.140 --> 14:05.890
Wait.

14:06.970 --> 14:08.530
Beethoven-senpai?

14:11.460 --> 14:13.430
I'm already back home.

14:14.050 --> 14:16.450
After all I went through to escape...

14:16.930 --> 14:18.790
But that doesn't matter anymore.

14:19.010 --> 14:21.660
You've chosen well,

14:21.660 --> 14:23.260
to have eaten my gyoza.

14:23.260 --> 14:24.790
I appreciate your spirit.

14:24.790 --> 14:25.660
Yes.

14:25.660 --> 14:27.800
Beethoven-senpai loves me now.

14:28.260 --> 14:30.240
He loves me. I'm in bliss.

14:30.240 --> 14:32.240
This is the happiest moment of my life.

14:32.240 --> 14:33.320
I'm content.

14:33.320 --> 14:36.490
It is, in fact, my deepest desire
to be eaten by Beethoven-senpai.

14:36.490 --> 14:38.730
I'll make sure he enjoys me to the fullest.

14:39.210 --> 14:41.860
I shall satiate his tongue
to the best of my ability.

14:42.380 --> 14:47.520
I shall live on as Beethoven-senpai's
flesh and blood!

14:51.520 --> 14:52.210
Huh?

14:53.950 --> 14:55.200
Where am I?

14:56.930 --> 14:59.100
You're the fish that I caught.

14:59.430 --> 15:01.190
Beethoven-senpai, is that you?

15:01.920 --> 15:02.850
And you're...

15:02.850 --> 15:04.030
Schubert, sir.

15:06.260 --> 15:09.260
So this is because of your Musik?

15:09.560 --> 15:11.210
Yes. I'm ecstatic.

15:11.210 --> 15:14.230
To think that I could be in
this situation with you.

15:14.230 --> 15:15.970
Don't you dare.

15:15.970 --> 15:17.220
Return me immediately.

15:17.220 --> 15:18.930
Do you want to be cooked into gyoza?

15:18.930 --> 15:20.020
W-Well...

15:20.020 --> 15:22.180
I don't know how to get back, either.

15:22.180 --> 15:23.150
What?!

15:23.830 --> 15:24.770
Oh, my.

15:25.120 --> 15:26.470
Hey, come quick.

15:26.470 --> 15:29.010
I found some tasty-looking fish.

15:29.010 --> 15:30.280
Guys!

15:31.020 --> 15:32.300
What's going on?

15:32.300 --> 15:34.160
Why are there fish popping in and out?

15:34.530 --> 15:36.490
Is this house connected to something?

15:36.790 --> 15:37.560
Huh?

15:37.840 --> 15:40.580
It looks kind of like the
one I set free at Lake Hamana.

15:40.900 --> 15:43.290
And there's another weird one now.

15:43.290 --> 15:44.940
What's this fish called?

15:44.940 --> 15:46.430
Black bass.

15:46.430 --> 15:48.460
One of eight species of largemouth bass,

15:48.460 --> 15:50.800
a carnivorous freshwater fish.

15:51.020 --> 15:52.240
Okay.

15:52.240 --> 15:53.880
Let's eat it.

15:54.730 --> 15:57.030
But there isn't enough for everyone.

15:57.030 --> 15:58.940
I'm sure there'll be more.

15:58.940 --> 16:00.980
I guess Beethes-san is catching them.

16:00.980 --> 16:03.730
I'm right here! Notice me! Hey!

16:03.990 --> 16:05.900
Hey, he's a lively one.

16:06.410 --> 16:07.740
It's no use, Senpai.

16:07.740 --> 16:10.200
They don't understand our language.

16:11.130 --> 16:12.940
Are our hands tied?

16:12.940 --> 16:14.780
Yes. Because we're fish, get it?

16:14.870 --> 16:18.450
Fish Recipes

16:16.100 --> 16:18.450
This looks so delicious.

16:18.740 --> 16:21.060
How should we have them?
Probably meunière, right?

16:21.060 --> 16:22.470
How about butter sauté?

16:22.470 --> 16:24.200
Karaage might be nice.

16:24.200 --> 16:26.050
You can't go wrong with salt-grilled.

16:26.050 --> 16:27.170
Cream stew.

16:28.070 --> 16:30.440
I'm willing to be cooked in any way.

16:30.440 --> 16:31.840
But Senpai...

16:31.840 --> 16:33.970
You must roast him whole

16:33.970 --> 16:37.100
to preserve his noble appearance!

16:37.710 --> 16:39.700
And he must reign over the center

16:39.700 --> 16:41.890
of the dinner table as the main dish.

16:42.350 --> 16:44.760
I ought to be sliced thin into a carpaccio.

16:44.760 --> 16:47.030
No, just mix me into a salad.

16:47.030 --> 16:48.270
But treat Senpai well!

16:48.500 --> 16:50.440
You want<i> to be eaten, don't you?</i>

16:50.440 --> 16:52.340
Are you sure about this?

16:53.150 --> 16:55.540
I don't intend to surrender to fate.

16:55.850 --> 16:58.030
Even if I'm chopped into three.

16:58.030 --> 17:01.700
I shall resist until the end!

17:02.060 --> 17:06.740
Spielen wir unsere Musik!

17:24.300 --> 17:25.520
What the hell?!

17:25.520 --> 17:27.650
Out of the way, predators!

17:29.750 --> 17:31.940
My freedom

17:32.900 --> 17:33.940
will not be obstructed!

17:34.170 --> 17:36.130
The fish is controlling it.

17:36.130 --> 17:39.300
So it isn't going to go down with a fight.

17:39.620 --> 17:42.330
Watch Out For Fire

17:40.460 --> 17:42.330
I like your spirit.

17:42.790 --> 17:43.500
Move!

17:43.800 --> 17:45.580
Make way!

17:46.110 --> 17:48.580
Beethoven-senpai! You're so awesome!

17:49.320 --> 17:52.100
Sorry, but love and hunger

17:52.100 --> 17:53.900
don't die down that easily.

17:53.900 --> 17:56.660
You're coming into my
stomach, my little fishies!

17:56.660 --> 17:58.300
Crab sounds good, too.

17:58.300 --> 18:00.100
I don't think this is edible.

18:00.330 --> 18:01.450
We're breaking out.

18:01.450 --> 18:01.850
Okay.

18:09.130 --> 18:11.070
You're not getting away,

18:11.070 --> 18:13.030
my dinner!

18:16.950 --> 18:19.190
They'll escape if they get outside.

18:19.190 --> 18:22.500
We're going to stop them here, tool!

18:23.620 --> 18:26.710
Heave, ho! Heave, ho!

18:26.710 --> 18:29.460
Heave, ho! Heave, ho!

18:27.400 --> 18:28.830
Pesky fools.

18:34.810 --> 18:37.050
Just outside that gate is freedom.

18:37.290 --> 18:39.050
We shall make freedom ours!

18:39.270 --> 18:40.890
I'll follow you anywhere.

19:03.080 --> 19:05.370
Serves you right, Mozart!

19:05.370 --> 19:06.340
And...

19:07.960 --> 19:11.610
That was beautiful, Beethoven-senpai!

19:23.880 --> 19:25.370
Good morning, everyone.

19:25.370 --> 19:27.000
I'm Schubert.

19:27.000 --> 19:30.390
It's time for another fun day of fish life!

19:31.640 --> 19:33.150
Beethoven-senpai.

19:33.600 --> 19:35.840
You're looking delightful, as always.

19:36.600 --> 19:37.870
Schubert, is that you?

19:40.120 --> 19:41.580
I'm so hungry.

19:41.580 --> 19:43.660
Yes, so am I.

19:43.950 --> 19:46.080
My, good day, you two.

19:46.080 --> 19:47.380
Miss Liszt.

19:47.380 --> 19:49.280
You're as beautiful as always.

19:49.280 --> 19:50.690
Why, thank you.

19:50.690 --> 19:53.060
Beautiful fish are poisonous, though.

19:53.580 --> 19:55.660
I'm so hungry, though.

19:55.660 --> 19:57.890
Yes, so am I.

19:57.890 --> 20:00.010
I'm getting bored of eating plankton.

20:01.710 --> 20:03.590
How's everyone doing?

20:04.000 --> 20:05.930
Motes is always doing great.

20:05.010 --> 20:07.310
I'm flying, I'm flying!

20:05.930 --> 20:07.310
I hate him.

20:07.790 --> 20:09.490
B-Be quiet.

20:09.490 --> 20:10.600
Oh, my, Cho-chan.

20:10.910 --> 20:12.000
Good morning.

20:12.000 --> 20:13.610
So many fish.

20:13.610 --> 20:14.490
I'm scared.

20:14.490 --> 20:16.390
You're a shy one.

20:16.390 --> 20:18.190
I'm so hungry, though.

20:18.190 --> 20:20.310
Yes, so am I.

20:20.310 --> 20:22.610
I'm getting bored of eating plankton.

20:23.090 --> 20:26.620
Hey, guys, there's some
tasty-looking moss here.

20:26.940 --> 20:28.890
Oh my, that does look tasty.

20:28.890 --> 20:30.370
Let's dig in.

20:32.380 --> 20:34.640
What tasty moss.

20:34.640 --> 20:36.410
Nom, nom. Yummy.

20:36.410 --> 20:38.590
We should live on this rock forever.

20:38.590 --> 20:41.360
Hey, no one said you could live here.

20:42.070 --> 20:43.260
What do you want, fry?

20:43.510 --> 20:45.260
This is my rock.

20:45.260 --> 20:47.430
You can't live here unless you pay rent.

20:47.770 --> 20:50.050
Rent? What are we supposed to pay with?

20:50.050 --> 20:51.640
I can only pay in poo.

20:51.640 --> 20:54.100
<i>You</i> figure it out.

20:54.100 --> 20:55.500
That's heavy-handed, fry!

20:55.500 --> 20:56.810
Stop calling me "fry!"

20:57.190 --> 20:58.590
Stop fighting.

20:58.590 --> 20:59.650
Aren't you friends?

20:59.950 --> 21:01.180
That rock talked!

21:01.180 --> 21:03.580
He's not a rock. He's a snail.

21:03.580 --> 21:05.260
He's been there the whole time.

21:05.260 --> 21:07.350
You aren't a fish, so stay out of this.

21:07.350 --> 21:08.030
What?

21:08.360 --> 21:11.680
Come on, we all live under the sea.

21:12.240 --> 21:15.620
Lion fish, flying fish, garden eel,

21:15.620 --> 21:17.750
clownfish, river snail.

21:18.230 --> 21:21.540
Really, though, when is
this going to be over?

21:21.540 --> 21:23.710
It's been a week already.

21:27.200 --> 21:28.940
Oh. They're back.

21:28.940 --> 21:30.220
Huh? What?

21:30.520 --> 21:31.880
What just happened?

21:31.880 --> 21:33.540
Where are the fish?

21:33.540 --> 21:34.790
Where's the crab robot?

21:34.790 --> 21:36.620
Why are we wet?

21:36.620 --> 21:39.030
I got home from fishing, and...

21:41.510 --> 21:44.150
And why are you naked?

21:44.150 --> 21:45.310
Why?

21:45.310 --> 21:47.500
Well, I was bathing.

21:46.780 --> 21:48.000
Ew!

21:48.000 --> 21:49.200
Pervert!

21:49.200 --> 21:50.840
Shut it! I'm no pervert!

21:50.840 --> 21:51.680
Pervert!

21:53.270 --> 21:53.970
Okay.

21:59.230 --> 22:01.250
What a strange thing to happen.

22:01.690 --> 22:03.880
I can't believe no one remembers.

22:04.730 --> 22:06.950
That was incredibly embarrassing.

22:07.760 --> 22:09.260
That aside, though...

22:09.550 --> 22:11.740
That was great, seeing Mozart depressed

22:11.740 --> 22:14.160
that he let his fish get away.

22:14.160 --> 22:16.080
Such superficial men deserve

22:16.080 --> 22:18.620
to be taken down a notch.

22:20.730 --> 22:22.250
Good job, fish!

22:44.000 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

24:15.970 --> 24:27.980
14: Claskey Klasky Breaks Up,
Kanae Makes Her Debut

24:16.160 --> 24:19.230
With the light of the sun,
the moon stands, quietly.

24:19.230 --> 24:20.650
Give me a break!

24:20.650 --> 24:24.310
Listen, the moon has bright
wishes, too, you know.

24:26.250 --> 24:29.230
Show them what a
one-hit wonder is made of.
